  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Peel and clean the root vegetables. Using a mandoline (or a knife), slice them thinly to about 0.25 cm."
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring a pot of water to the boil. Add the soaked lentils and cook for 8 to 10 minutes. Drain and set aside."
    },
    {
      "text": "In a wide, shallow pot, lightly fry the chopped onion until golden and translucent. Add the garlic, celery stalks cut into sticks, chilli, ginger slices, black pepper and cardamom and stir for about 1 minute. Add the lentils and 1 litre of boiling water and stir. Cook over medium heat for 10 minutes. Add the spinach and the salt and stir."
    },
    {
      "text": "Five minutes before serving, add the sliced root vegetables."
    }
  ]
